    "TREATMENT": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Generally not serious debilitating disorder if truly BVS, but important to rule out major conditions such as gastritis, IBD, or GI",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "neoplasia.",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Idiopathic bilious vomiting cases generally treated symptomatically on an outpatient basis and treatment response",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "supports suspected diagnosis.",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Feeding the animal small frequent meals, including late evening meal, often resolves clinical signs; food possibly could act as buffer to refluxed bile or may in some way enhance GI motility.",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Trial with hypoallergenic diet (novel protein or hydrolyzed protein) can also improve clinical signs, which may actually suggest",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "underlying food‐responsive enteropathy.",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "If diet modification fails, medical treatment should be considered.",
          "pdf_page": 261,
          "printed_page": 179,
          "column": 2
        }
      ],
